::PC_U03_L06_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U03_L06_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.TR.13
Question:
Which statement correctly identifies a trigonometric graph feature?
{
~A. The period of y=sin(x) is pi.#The basic sine period is 2pi.
~B. The midline of y=cos(x)+2 is y=0.#The +2 shifts the midline to y=2.
~C. The range of y=3sin(x) is all real numbers.#Sine range is bounded by amplitude.
=D. The amplitude of y=4sin(x) is 4.#Correct. The coefficient 4 gives the sine amplitude.
}
